WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.680
How do I put a site online with AWS without leaving

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.430
anything open by mistake?

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.750
That's today's question.

4
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:07.720
It takes about an hour.

5
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.850
And you can do the first three steps without an account.

6
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.170
Before asking AI, write down what you think.

7
00:00:13.553 --> 00:00:16.533
Paste this request into your AI assistant.

8
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:17.973
Notice the last item.

9
00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:21.373
You ask for the official documentation link behind each

10
00:00:21.373 --> 00:00:24.593
answer. Then comes the most important part of the mission:

11
00:00:24.593 --> 00:00:25.903
opening those links.

12
00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:27.853
It's not enough for a link to exist.

13
00:00:27.853 --> 00:00:29.783
It has to say what the AI claimed.

14
00:00:30.153 --> 00:00:32.703
An AI may suggest a public S3 bucket.

15
00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:35.503
Look at what the S3 documentation itself says.

16
00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:38.743
That path requires turning off Block Public Access.

17
00:00:38.993 --> 00:00:40.863
It also recommends keeping that block on.

18
00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:43.843
And it warns that the S3 website only has HTTP.

19
00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:45.283
Did your AI tell you that?

20
00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:47.423
Write down what matched and what didn't.

21
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.760
Now download the mission's page and replace the text with

22
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.360
yours. Run this command and open it in your browser.

23
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:58.160
Ask AI to review the clarity, without writing it for you.

24
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.800
And be careful: don't include your phone,

25
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.610
your address or anything you don't want public.

26
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:05.547
If you already have an account,

27
00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:06.937
publish with Amplify.

28
00:01:07.087 --> 00:01:08.547
Put the file in a zip.

29
00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:11.787
Zip the file, not the folder, because zipping the folder

30
00:01:11.787 --> 00:01:13.777
causes an access denied error.

31
00:01:14.027 --> 00:01:16.747
In the console, create an app without Git,

32
00:01:16.747 --> 00:01:18.517
drop the zip and save.

33
00:01:18.707 --> 00:01:21.327
In our test, it took about 48 s,

34
00:01:21.327 --> 00:01:25.037
and the site answered over HTTPS with no extra setup.

35
00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:28.557
An honest caveat. That test ran from the command line,

36
00:01:28.557 --> 00:01:30.887
with the same kind of zip upload.

37
00:01:31.237 --> 00:01:33.577
The console clicks follow the documentation,

38
00:01:33.577 --> 00:01:35.887
but they weren't tested step by step.

39
00:01:36.097 --> 00:01:37.977
If something looks different on your screen,

40
00:01:37.977 --> 00:01:40.087
write it down. That's evidence too.

41
00:01:40.453 --> 00:01:42.713
If the site was just a test, delete it.

42
00:01:42.713 --> 00:01:46.333
In the Amplify console, open the app and go to settings,

43
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:48.143
to the option that deletes the app.

44
00:01:48.493 --> 00:01:51.203
Then open the address again and confirm it's offline.

45
00:01:51.493 --> 00:01:53.813
The cost is normally zero at this size,

46
00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:57.003
but check your account, because the free tier changes.

47
00:01:57.487 --> 00:01:59.347
And now you have a story to tell.

48
00:01:59.347 --> 00:02:02.587
You compared what AI suggested with what the documentation

49
00:02:02.587 --> 00:02:05.727
says. You published a site with HTTPS.

50
00:02:05.727 --> 00:02:07.937
And you cleaned up at the end.

51
00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.007
That's an article you can write on your own,

52
00:02:10.007 --> 00:02:11.107
in your own words.

53
00:02:11.107 --> 00:02:12.577
AI only reviews.

54
00:02:12.953 --> 00:02:14.933
One note before we finish.

55
00:02:14.933 --> 00:02:17.533
The voice you just heard was generated from my cloned

56
00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:19.573
voice, with my authorization.

57
00:02:19.573 --> 00:02:21.553
And this is an independent project.

58
00:02:21.553 --> 00:02:24.423
It is not official AWS material.
